I implemented the node but left out both operations additions.

- **Log file:** the target is `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI adapter, so there is no filesystem to write `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` to.
- **Metadata fetch:** the node is declared with only `inference-llm`. Calling `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q=<input text>` would need an `http-client` import, which is authority the node was not granted. It would also send feed text, which is untrusted and adversarial, into a URL.

If you want either one, add it to the node's declared capabilities in the graph, for example an `http-client` allowlist or a log-sink interface, and I can wire it in.

